{{!
    @template tool_vae/state_legend

    The legend of the states of a declaration, as a fold: its heading, then one line per state, the word in bold and what
    it means (one end of line after the opening of the list and after each item, as the writer of the core put them).

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\state_legend. The template holds no logic. Every
    value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * heading - string, the heading of the fold
    * items - array of {state, help}: the word of a state and what it means

    Example context (json):
    {
        "heading": "What the states mean",
        "items": [
            {"state": "Declared", "help": "Written by the vaeiste, not attested yet."},
            {"state": "Attested", "help": "A manager signed it."}
        ]
    }
}}
<details class="tool-vae-legend mb-3"><summary>{{heading}}</summary><ul>
{{#items}}<li><strong>{{state}}</strong> - {{help}}</li>
{{/items}}</ul></details>
